---
description: Persistent engineering rules for the B2B Lead Intelligence SaaS
alwaysApply: true
---
- Read `README.md` and relevant `docs/` before implementing a feature.
- Do not silently change architecture decisions, schemas, API contracts or product scope.
- Implement small vertical slices and run checks after each change.
- Treat PostgreSQL as canonical truth; search and graph stores are derived projections.
- Enforce tenant authorization at every service boundary and test cross-tenant access.
- Every sourced company/person/contact/signal claim must have provenance.
- Label model inference distinctly from source/provider facts.
- Do not invent source citations, current roles, reporting lines, email addresses or buying intent.
- Use provider adapters and deterministic mocks. No credentials are required for local development.
- Do not implement anti-bot evasion, CAPTCHA bypass or unauthorized authenticated scraping.
- Do not use direct SMTP recipient probing as the default email verification method.
- Suppression overrides all scoring, export and outreach behavior.
- Do not send outreach automatically. Generate drafts for human review.
- Bound retries, pages, tokens, provider spend, job duration and concurrency.
- Validate all AI/provider outputs against schemas before persistence.
- Keep API contracts versioned and document breaking changes.
- Do not claim production readiness or scale capacity without test evidence.
- Never commit secrets, real contact data, production logs or private source dumps.
